## Pull request approvals

Every PR in an `example-org/*` repo should get approvals from two different
reviewers before it merges. GitHub doesn't enforce it: `reviewDecision`
reads `APPROVED` after the first approval, so don't rely on it.

- Report review status as a count, e.g. "1 of 2 approvals". Only call a PR
  approved or ready to merge once it has two.
